CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ copy-init decl in pack body: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.init]/15-16: a block-scope `S x = "s";` copy-initialization in
a variadic function-template body.  The pack expander used to CREATE an
empty ID_init_args entry on every declarator it visited (irept::add
creates-on-absence); typecheck_decl then crashed on "declarator should
not have init_args".  Found by dog-fooding CBMC's own util/invariant.h
(std::string backtrace = ... in the variadic report_invariant_failure
chain); reduced with cvise + manual bisection.  Header-free; g++/clang++
runtime-verified.
